  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nIt's pretty common across desktop apps to use CTRL or SHIFT as UP ARROW and DOWN ARROW modifier for `<input type=\"number\">` incrementing. \n\nfor example in developer tools putting focus in an input and pressing up increments the value by 1 by default but adding SHIFT to UP changes the increment value to 10, while using CTRL and UP increments by .1\n\nIt would be nice if this sort of thing was built into `<input type=\"number\">`. Begin able to control what each modifier did would also be great.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n_No response_\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
